Troubleshoot: common failures and cleanup

Match the symptom, run the named check, apply the named fix.
Privileged steps below are code-read only; they were not run here
beyond unprivileged doctor and lint. CLI lives at cmd/main.c.

TUN permission denied

No TUN means no mesh, so runs skip instead of failing.

Symptom: suite why holds skip (errno
text) with stdout suite: skip <name>
(errno text) (suite/exec.c:8067-8082),
or sim prints skip (errno) on host tun
open (sim/sim.c:971-974), or check TUN
tests print tun_netns: skip (errno) and
tun_drop: skip (errno)
(check/tun_netns.c:45,
check/tun_drop.c:45). Errno is often
Permission denied.

Confirm with bin/rsuite doctor
(cmd/main.c:2465-2520): read euid root,
/dev/net/tun, and netns list lines.
MISSING (not root) plus MISSING (no tun
access) point here. Doctor exits 0
with the report even then; 1 only on
probe error.

Fix: rerun with root for netns plus
TUN, as in bin/rsuite run which needs
root (docs/overview commands).
Silent make test skips are expected
without privs (test recipe in the
Makefile, docs/layer5-runner:79-88);
they are not failures.

Docker absent

Weld needs docker, concord does not.

Symptom on weld files only: why holds
skip no docker with stdout suite: skip
<name> no docker (suite/exec.c:7971-7984).
Probe runs docker info with a bound;
missing, failing, or hung daemon counts
as must-skip, never a stall
(driver/weld.c:508-562). Doctor shows
docker daemon MISSING (daemon down)
(cmd/main.c:2499-2500).

Fix: start the docker daemon, confirm
doctor says OK, rerun. Concord files
are unaffected; only the weld branch
checks docker (suite/exec.c:7950-7984).
Do not rebuild images; this is daemon
presence, not image content.

Binary missing

No binary means nothing to run, so runs skip.

Concord symptom: why holds skip no
<bin> with stdout suite: skip <name> no
<bin> when access X_OK fails on
./bin/concord or SuiteOpts concord_bin
(suite/exec.c:7930-7949, access in
7936). Check shape is the same: skip no
./bin/concord (e.g. check/concord_two
path). Weld symptom is the same bytes
via weld_skip_unless_bin, null means
default path (driver/weld.c:497-505,
suite/exec.c:7951-7970).

Fix: build ./bin/concord by hand from a Concord checkout
(cd deps/concord && go build -o $PWD/bin/concord ./cmd/concord).
For image tests also run make img-build
to fill img/rootfs with probe plus
probe-check offline; concord_img needs those bins at run
time. Then rerun.
Do not edit YAML to dodge the skip.

Port and route collisions

Two host runs fight over one host route and one port.

Symptom: second run fails setup or
flaps while first still lives. Cause:
two runs with a host node both claim
the host 224.0.0.0/4 route and both
bind port 7946 (sim/sim.c:364-368,
docs/speed:40-44). Memberlist binds
0.0.0.0:7946 with advertise and anchor
addrs at under.octet:7946
(sim/sim.c:1422-1449).

Fix: run isolated or serial. Isolated
runs with distinct nets share only the
allocator file (run/run.c:585-591).
Executor always selects isolated with
per-run statedir, ns prefix, tun base,
octet, and cgroot (suite/exec.c:8026-8029,
sim/sim.c:372-410). Check files keep
host node 0 and stay serial and frozen
(docs/speed:40-44). If colliding, stop
one run or move both to bin/rsuite run
which isolates.

Full stale-state cleanup recipe

Dead runs leave names, dirs, and ids behind. Remove them in this
order. All privileged lines are code-read only from teardown and
setup paths; they were not executed here.

1. Netns names. List with ip netns list,
then delete each resonance name with
ip netns del <name>. Source adds with
ip netns add <prefix><i> after del for
retry (sim/sim.c:760-770) and deletes
one by one in teardown
(sim/sim.c:869-922). Filter for the
resonance prefix only; do not delete
other names.

2. Cgroup subtree. Teardown runs rmdir
on each <cgroot>/node<i> then on
<cgroot> with stderr nulled, empty only
(sim/sim.c:896-922). By hand remove
leaves first, code-read only:

sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance/node*/daemon 2>/dev/null
sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance/node* 2>/dev/null
sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance 2>/dev/null
sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance-*/node*/daemon 2>/dev/null
sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance-*/node* 2>/dev/null
sudo rmdir /sys/fs/cgroup/resonance-* 2>/dev/null

Rmdir removes empty dirs only, so
strays fail silently by design. Do not
use rm -rf on cgroupfs.

3. Statedirs. Teardown wipes with
rm -rf <statedir> after revalid plus
netns delete (run/run.c:790-799). By
hand, code-read only:

sudo rm -rf /var/tmp/resonance
sudo rm -rf /var/tmp/resonance-*

Restart also wipes one node dir with
rm -rf <statedir>/node<i>
(sim/sim.c:1740-1747). Forensics aside
dirs live beside statedir at
<statedir>-fail/suite-<secs>
(suite/exec.c:7785-7789) and survive
the wipe; remove them only when done
with post-mortem:

sudo rm -rf /var/tmp/resonance-fail /var/tmp/resonance-*-fail

4. Allocator lock files. Ids recycle
when their run exits: the winner fd is
held open till process exit, so crash
and kill both free the id with the fd.
No manual reset exists. If every id
reports busy, live runs hold them; wait
or reboot. A stale
/var/tmp/resonance-runs.counter from an
older build is inert; remove it once by
hand:

sudo rm -f /var/tmp/resonance-runs.counter
sudo rm -f /var/tmp/resonance-runs.counter.tmp.*

Leave /var/tmp/resonance-runs.lock and
/var/tmp/resonance-run-N.lock files in
place. Doctor checks lock R plus W, a
free run id, and lock dir W plus X.

5. Rsuite log dirs. Fresh per-run dir
under /var/tmp via mkdtemp
/var/tmp/resonance-rsuite-XXXXXX
(cmd/main.c:689-702) with per-file
<base>.log plus <base>-N.log on clash
(cmd/main.c:764-807). Nothing cleans
them by design (cmd/main.c:364-405).
By hand when done reading them:

rm -rf /var/tmp/resonance-rsuite-*
rm -rf <any custom --log-dir run dir>

Check size first with du -sh.

6. Img tmp files. Per-process scratch
/tmp/resonance-img-<pid>-<name> for
hdrs, body, hdump, code
(img/img.c:85-92,106,155-157) plus
per-push -layer.tar, -config.json,
-manifest.json (img/img.c:232-240). No
auto unlink. By hand:

rm -f /tmp/resonance-img-*

Post-mortem path

Failed runs save clues before wiping. Read the clues in this order.

1. Rerun or keep IMG_DEBUG=1 for image
push detail. When set, put_manifest
prints [img] manifest code, body, and
hdrs lines (img/img.c:174-196). Use it
for diagnosis only; suite default stays
quiet.

2. Find the forensics dir line on
stderr: suite: forensics at <dir>
(suite/exec.c:7837-7839). Dir is
<statedir>-fail/suite-<secs> with
copies of weld plus ros logs on weld,
or journal plus config plus node logs
on concord (suite/exec.c:7794-7828).
Open that dir; the live statedir is
already wiped by run_teardown
(run/run.c:790-799).

3. Read per-node log tails. Forensics
prints --- <log-path> plus bytes for
each node log, or no <log-path> when
missing (suite/exec.c:7706-7747). Concord
tails <statedir>/node-<i>.log; weld
tails <statedir>/weld-<i>.log plus
<statedir>/ros-<i>.log where a peer runs
(suite/exec.c:7770-7784, log_path in
4572-4586). Grep those tails for
"level":"error" plus peers markers as
check forensics does
(docs/layer4-observation:26-33), then
open the full per-file log in the
rsuite run dir for phase context.
